([Sidenote: Of parents' wills.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Children are not, ordinarily, called of God to marry, when their) Tj T*
(parents do absolutely and peremptorily forbid it. For though parents') Tj T*
(commands cannot make it a duty, when we are sure it would hinder the) Tj T*
(interest of God our ultimate end; yet parents' prohibitions may make) Tj T*
(it a sin, when there is a clear probability that it would most conduce) Tj T*
(to our ultimate end, were it not prohibited. Because, \(1.\)) Tj T*
(Affirmatives bind not _semper et ad semper_, as negatives or) Tj T*
(prohibitions do. \(2.\) Because the sin of disobedience to parents will) Tj T*
(cross the tendency of it unto good, and do more against our ultimate) Tj T*
