(little to satisfy those that you provide for, you will measure your) Tj T*
(estate by their desires, and be apt to think that you have never) Tj T*
(enough. Birds and beasts that have young ones to provide for, are most) Tj T*
(hungry and rapacious. You have so many now to scrape for, that you) Tj T*
(will think you are still in want: it is not only till death that you) Tj T*
(must now lay up; but you must provide for children that survive you.) Tj T*
(And while you take them to be as yourselves, you have two generations) Tj T*
(now to make provisions for: and most men are as covetous for their) Tj T*
(posterity, as if it were for themselves.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
