(CHAPTER IV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(GENERAL DIRECTIONS FOR THE HOLY GOVERNMENT OF FAMILIES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE principal thing requisite to the right governing of families, is) Tj T*
(the fitness of the governors and the governed thereto, which is spoken) Tj T*
(of before in the directions for the constitution. But if persons unfit) Tj T*
(for their relations, have joined themselves together in a family,) Tj T*
(their first duty is to repent of their former sin and rashness, and) Tj T*
(presently to turn to God, and seek after that fitness which is) Tj T*
(necessary to the right discharge of the duties of their several) Tj T*
(places: and in the governors of families, these three things are of) Tj T*
(greatest necessity hereunto: I. Authority. II. Skill. III. Holiness) Tj T*
(and readiness of will.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: How to keep up authority.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I. _Gen. Direct._ Let governors maintain their authority in their) Tj T*
(families. For if once that be lost, and you are despised by those that) Tj T*
(you should rule, your word will be of no effect with them; you do but) Tj T*
(ride without a bridle; your power of governing is gone, when your) Tj T*
(authority is lost. And here you must first understand the nature, use,) Tj T*
(and extent of your authority; for as your relations are different, to) Tj T*
(your wife, your children, and your servants, so also is your) Tj T*
(authority. Your authority over your wife, is but such as is necessary) Tj T*
(to the order of your family, the safe and prudent management of your) Tj T*
(affairs, and your comfortable cohabitation. The power of love and) Tj T*
(complicated interest must do more than magisterial commands. Your) Tj T*
(authority over your children is much greater; but yet only such as,) Tj T*
(conjunct with love, is needful to their good education and felicity.) Tj T*
(Your authority over your servants is to be measured by your contract) Tj T*
(with them \(in these countries where there are no slaves\) in order to) Tj T*
(your service, and the honour of God. In other matters, or to other) Tj T*
