() Tj T*
(CHAPTER V.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SPECIAL MOTIVES TO PERSUADE MEN TO THE HOLY GOVERNING OF THEIR) Tj T*
(FAMILIES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(IF it were but well understood what benefits come by the holy) Tj T*
(governing of families, and what mischiefs come by its neglect, there) Tj T*
(would few that walk the streets among us, appear so odious as those) Tj T*
(careless, ungodly governors that know not nor mind a duty of such) Tj T*
(exceeding weight. While we lie all as overwhelmed with the calamitous) Tj T*
(fruits of this neglect, I think meet to try if, with some, the cause) Tj T*
(may be removed, by awakening sluggish souls to do their undertaken) Tj T*
(work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Motive_ I. Consider that the holy government of families, is a) Tj T*
(considerable part of God's own government of the world, and the) Tj T*
(contrary is a great part of the devil's government. It hath pleased) Tj T*
(God to settle as a natural, so a political order in the world, and to) Tj T*
(honour his creatures to be the instruments of his own operations; and) Tj T*
(though he could have produced all effects without any inferior causes,) Tj T*
(and could have governed the world by himself alone without any) Tj T*
