(their young, to cherish them till they can go abroad and shift for) Tj T*
(themselves, for corporal sustenance? It is not dogs or beasts that you) Tj T*
(bring into the world, but children that have immortal souls; and) Tj T*
(therefore it is a care and education suitable to their natures which) Tj T*
(you owe them; even such as conduceth most effectually to the happiness) Tj T*
(of their souls. Nature teacheth them some natural things without you,) Tj T*
(as it doth the bird to fly; but it hath committed it to your trust and) Tj T*
(care to teach them the greatest and most necessary things: if you) Tj T*
