(quench affection, and not to get assistance from another, it is wisdom) Tj T*
(to conceal it; but that is not the ordinary case. The opening your) Tj T*
(hearts to each other is necessary to your mutual help.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ X. Avoid as much as may be contrariety of opinions in) Tj T*
(religion: for if once you be of different judgments in matters which) Tj T*
(you take to be of great concernment, you will be tempted to disaffect,) Tj T*
(contemn, or undervalue one another; and so to despise the help which) Tj T*
(you might receive: and if you fall into several sects, and follow) Tj T*
(several teachers, you will hardly avoid that contention and confusion,) Tj T*
(which will prove a great advantage to the devil, and a great) Tj T*
(impediment to your spiritual good.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ XI. If difference in judgment in matters of religion do) Tj T*
(fall out between you, be sure that it be managed with holiness,) Tj T*
(humility, love, and peace, and not with carnality, pride,) Tj T*
(uncharitableness, or contention. 1. To manage your differences holily,) Tj T*
(is to take God for the judge, and to refer the matter to his word, and) Tj T*
(to aim at his glory, and the pleasing of his will, and to use his) Tj T*
(means for the concord of your judgments; which is, to search the) Tj T*
(Scripture, and consult with the faithful, able pastors of the church,) Tj T*
(and soberly and patiently to debate the case, and pray together for) Tj T*
(the illumination of the Spirit. On the contrary your differences are) Tj T*
(carnally managed, when carnal reasons breed or feed them; and when you) Tj T*
(run after this or that sect or party, through admiration of the) Tj T*
(persons; and value not the persons for the sake of truth, but measure) Tj T*
(truth by the opinion and estimate of the persons; and when you end) Tj T*
(your differences by selfish, carnal principles and respects: and hence) Tj T*
(it comes to pass, that if the husband be a papist or otherwise) Tj T*
(erroneous, it is two to one that the wife becometh of his erroneous) Tj T*
(religion, not because of any cogent evidence, but because he is of the) Tj T*
(stronger parts, and hath constant opportunity to persuade, and because) Tj T*
(love prepareth and inclineth her to be of his opinion: and thus man,) Tj T*
(instead of God, is the master of the faith of many. 2. Your) Tj T*
(differences are managed in humility, when you have a just and modest) Tj T*
(suspicion of your own understandings, and debate and practise your) Tj T*
(differences with meekness and submission; and do not proudly overvalue) Tj T*
(all your own apprehensions, and despise another's reasons as if they) Tj T*
