() Tj T*
(III. Those actions are out of our power, which are acts of higher) Tj T*
(authority than we have. A subject cannot reform by such actions as are) Tj T*
(proper to the sovereign, nor a layman by actions proper to the pastor,) Tj T*
(for want of authority. So a schoolmaster cannot do that which is) Tj T*
(proper to a patient; nor the master of a family that which is proper) Tj T*
(to the magistrate \(as to punish with death, &c.\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(IV. We have not power to do that which a superior power forbiddeth us) Tj T*
(\(unless it be that which God indispensably commandeth us\). The wife) Tj T*
(may not correct a child or servant, or turn him away, when the husband) Tj T*
(forbiddeth it. Nor the master of a family so punish a sin, as the king) Tj T*
(and laws forbid on the account of the public interest.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(V. We have not power to do that for the cure of sin, which is like to) Tj T*
(do more hurt than good; yea, perhaps, to prove a pernicious mischief.) Tj T*
(If my correcting a servant would make him kill me, or set my house on) Tj T*
(fire, I may not do it. If my sharp reproof is like to do more hurt, or) Tj T*
(less good, than milder dealing, if I have reason to believe that) Tj T*
(correction will make a servant worse, I am not to use it; because we) Tj T*
(have our power to edification, and not to destruction. God hath not) Tj T*
(tied us just to speak such and such words, or to use this or that) Tj T*
(correction, but to use reproofs and corrections only in that time,) Tj T*
(measure, and manner as true reason telleth us is likest to attain) Tj T*
(their end. To do it, if it would do never so much hurt, with a _fiat) Tj T*
(justitia etsi peruit mundus_, is to be righteous over-much.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Yea, great and heinous sins may be endured in families sometimes, to) Tj T*
(avoid a greater hurt, and because there is no other means to cure) Tj T*
(them. For instance, a wife maybe guilty of notorious pride, and of) Tj T*
(malignant deriding the exercises of religion, and of railing, lying,) Tj T*
(slandering, backbiting, covetousness, swearing, cursing, &c. and the) Tj T*
(husband be necessitated to bear it; not so far as not to reprove it,) Tj T*
(but so far as not to correct her, much less cure her. Divines use to) Tj T*
(say, that it is unlawful for a man to beat his wife: but the reason is) Tj T*
(not, that he wanteth authority to do it; but, 1. Because he is by his) Tj T*
