(to him all that is yours, and in your power; and therefore your) Tj T*
(children, as far as they are in your power. And as nature hath taught) Tj T*
(you your power and your duty to enter them in their infancy into any) Tj T*
(covenant with man, which is certainly for their good; \(and if they) Tj T*
(refuse the conditions when they come to age, they forfeit the) Tj T*
(benefit;\) so nature teacheth you much more to oblige them to God for) Tj T*
(their far greater good, in case he will admit them into covenant with) Tj T*
(him. And that he will admit them into his covenant, \(and that you) Tj T*
(ought to enter them into it,\) is past doubt, in the evidence which the) Tj T*
(Scripture giveth us, that from Abraham's time till Christ it was so) Tj T*
(with all the children of his people; nay, no man can prove that before) Tj T*
(Abraham's time, or since, God had ever a church on earth, of which the) Tj T*
(infants of his servants \(if they had any\) were not members dedicated) Tj T*
(in covenant to God, till of late times that a few began to scruple the) Tj T*
