(about, they are presently out of breath, and are a burden to) Tj T*
(themselves, and few of them live out little more than half their) Tj T*
(days. Whereas, poor creatures, if their own parents had not betrayed) Tj T*
(them into the sins of Sodom, pride, fulness of bread, and abundance of) Tj T*
(idleness, they might have been in health, and lived like honest) Tj T*
(christian people, and their legs and arms might have served them for) Tj T*
