(their parents?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Answ._ There are several acts and degrees of parents' government,) Tj T*
(according to the several ends and uses of it. Some acts of their) Tj T*
(government are but to teach you to go and speak, and some to teach you) Tj T*
(your labour and calling, and some to teach you good manners, and the) Tj T*
(fear of God, or the knowledge of the Scriptures, and some are to) Tj T*
(settle you in such a course of living, in which you shall need their) Tj T*
(nearer oversight no more. When any one of these ends are fully) Tj T*
(attained, and you have all that your parents' government can help you) Tj T*
(to, then you are past that part of their government. But still you owe) Tj T*
(them, not only love, and honour, and reverence; but obedience also in) Tj T*
(all things in which they are still appointed for your help and) Tj T*
(guidance: even when you are married from them, though you have a) Tj T*
(propriety in your own estates, and they have not so strict a charge of) Tj T*
