(ill-disposed to it, no wicked man would be bound to any thing that is) Tj T*
(truly holy. 2. And if heart and tongue be both obliged, it is worse to) Tj T*
(omit both than one. 3. And there may be sincerity in a duty, when the) Tj T*
(heart is cold and dull. 4. And beginning to do your duty as well as) Tj T*
