(brief directions for the holy spending of every day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ I. Proportion the time of your sleep aright, \(if it be) Tj T*
(in your power,\) that you waste not your precious morning hours) Tj T*
(sluggishly in your bed. Let the time of your sleep be rationally) Tj T*
(fitted to your health and labour, and not sensually to your slothful) Tj T*
(pleasure. About six hours is meet for healthful people, and seven) Tj T*
(hours for the less healthful, and eight for the more weak and aged,) Tj T*
(ordinarily. The morning hours are to most the preciousest of all) Tj T*
(the day, for all our duties; especially servants that are scanted of) Tj T*
(time, must take it then for prayer, if possible, lest they have none) Tj T*
(at all.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
