(be to-day for aught I know.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ V. Remember that all these days and sermons must be) Tj T*
(reviewed, and you must answer for all that you have heard, whether you) Tj T*
(heard it with love, or with unwillingness and weariness, with diligent) Tj T*
(attention or with carelessness; and the word which you hear shall) Tj T*
(judge you at the last day. Hear therefore as those that are going to) Tj T*
(judgment to give account of their hearing and obeying, John xii. 48.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ VI. Make it your work with diligence to apply the word) Tj T*
(as you are hearing it, and to work your own hearts to those suitable) Tj T*
(resolutions and affections which it bespeaketh. Cast not all upon the) Tj T*
(minister, as those that will go no further than they are carried as by) Tj T*
(force: this is fitter for the dead than for the living. You have work) Tj T*
(to do as well as the preacher, and should all the while be as busy as) Tj T*
(he: as helpless as the infant is, he must suck when the mother) Tj T*
(offereth him the breast; if you must be fed, yet you must open your) Tj T*
(mouths, and digest it, for another cannot digest it for you; nor can) Tj T*
