(for their own deliverance. Therefore be all the while at work, and) Tj T*
(abhor an idle heart in hearing, as well as an idle minister.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ VII. Chew the cud, and call up all when you come home) Tj T*
(in secret, and by meditation preach it over to yourselves. If it were) Tj T*
(coldly delivered by the preacher, do you consider of the great weight) Tj T*
(of the matter, and preach it more earnestly over to your own hearts.) Tj T*
(You should love yourselves best, and best be acquainted with your own) Tj T*
(condition and necessities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
