(under the wrath of God, and had been lost for ever, but that God of) Tj T*
(his mercy provided us a Redeemer, even the eternal Son of God; who) Tj T*
(being one with the Father, was pleased to take the nature of man, and) Tj T*
(so is both God and man in one person; who being born of a virgin,) Tj T*
(lived among men, and fulfilled the law of God, and overcame the) Tj T*
(tempter and the world, and died as a sacrifice for our sins, to) Tj T*
(reconcile us unto God. That all men being born with corrupted natures,) Tj T*
(and living in sin till Christ recover them, there is now no hope of) Tj T*
(salvation but by him. That he hath paid our debt, and made) Tj T*
(satisfaction for our sins, and risen from the dead, and conquered) Tj T*
(death and Satan, and is ascended and glorified in heaven; and that he) Tj T*
(is the King, and Teacher, and High Priest of the church. That he hath) Tj T*
(made a new covenant of grace and pardon, and offered it in the) Tj T*
(Scriptures and by his ministers to the world; and that those that are) Tj T*
