(performance of a condition, without which he hath not promised us his) Tj T*
(mercy, and to which he hath promised it. 3. As a means to actuate, and) Tj T*
(express, and increase our own humility, dependence, desire, trust, and) Tj T*
(hope in God, and so to make us capable and fit for mercy, who else) Tj T*
(should be uncapable and unfit. 4. And so, though God be not changed by) Tj T*
