(So that it is apparent that the method of the Lord's prayer is) Tj T*
(circular, partly analytical, and partly synthetical; beginning with) Tj T*
(God, and ending in God: beginning with such acknowledgments as are) Tj T*
(prerequisite to petition, and ending in those praises which petition) Tj T*
(and grace bestowed tend to: beginning our petitions for God's interest) Tj T*
(and the public good, according to the order of estimation and) Tj T*
(intention, till we come to the mere means, and then beginning at the) Tj T*
(lowest, and ascending according to the order of execution. As the) Tj T*
(blood passing from the greater to the smaller numerous vessels, is) Tj T*
(there received by the like, and repasseth to its fountain; such a) Tj T*
(circular method hath mercy and duty, and consequently our desires.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Tit. 2. Some Questions about Prayer answered._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
