() Tj T*
(_Quest._ VI. If both ways be lawful, which is better?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Answ._ If you are to join with others in the church, that is) Tj T*
(better to you which the pastor then useth: for it is his office and) Tj T*
(not yours to word the prayers which he puts up to God. And if he) Tj T*
(choose a form, \(whether it be as most agreeable to his parts, or to) Tj T*
(his people, or for concord with other churches, or for obedience to) Tj T*
(governors, or to avoid some greater inconvenience,\) you must join with) Tj T*
(him, or not join there at all.[59] But if it be in private, where you) Tj T*
(are the speaker yourself, you must take that way that is most to your) Tj T*
(own edification \(and to others, if you have auditors joining with) Tj T*
