(to all; and thus those that are not regenerate are his children by) Tj T*
(creation, and by participation of his mercy; and they may both call) Tj T*
(him Father and pray to himself, though yet they are unregenerate.[60]) Tj T*
(2. God hath an interest in you, when you have no special interest in) Tj T*
(him: therefore his command must be obeyed which bids you pray. 3.) Tj T*
(Groundless doubts will not disoblige you from your duty; else men) Tj T*
(might free themselves from almost all their obedience.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Quest._ XI. May a wicked or unregenerate man pray, and is he) Tj T*
(accepted? Or is not his prayer abominable to God?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Answ._ 1. A wicked man as a wicked man, can pray no how but) Tj T*
