(_Quest._ XIII. Is it idolatry to pray to saints or angels? or is) Tj T*
(it always sinful?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Answ._ I love not to be too quarrelsome with other men's) Tj T*
(devotions; but, 1. I see not how praying to an angel or a departed) Tj T*
(saint can be excused from sin.[63] Because it supposeth them to be) Tj T*
(every where present, or to be omniscient, and to know the heart, yea,) Tj T*
(to know at once the hearts of all men; or else the speaker pretendeth) Tj T*
(to know when the saint or angel is present and heareth him, and when) Tj T*
(not: and because the Scripture doth no where signify that God would) Tj T*
(have us pray to any such saints or angels; but signifieth enough to) Tj T*
(satisfy us of the contrary. 2. But all prayer to them is not idolatry,) Tj T*
(but some is, and therefore we must distinguish, if we will judge) Tj T*
(righteously. \(1.\) To pray to saints or angels as supposed omnipresent,) Tj T*
(omniscient, or omnipotent, is flat idolatry. \(2.\) To pray to them to) Tj T*
(forgive us our sins against God, or to justify, or sanctify, or) Tj T*
