(wicked men whose presence is your sin, because you have power to) Tj T*
(remove them, and those whose presence is not your sin, nor the matter) Tj T*
(in your power. 4. And between one that may yet choose of what family) Tj T*
(he will be, and one that may not. And so I answer, \(1.\) If it be the) Tj T*
(fault of the master of the family \(or the pastors of the church\) that) Tj T*
(such wicked men are there, and not cast out, then it is their sin to) Tj T*
(join with them, because it is their duty to remove them; but that is) Tj T*
(not the case of the fellow-servants, \(or people,\) that have no power.) Tj T*
(\(2.\) If that wicked men profess their wickedness, after sufficient) Tj T*
