(_Tit. 2. Directions for preventing Backsliding, or for Perseverance._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Apostasy and backsliding is a state that is more easily prevented than) Tj T*
(cured; and therefore I shall desire those that stand, to use these) Tj T*
(following directions, lest they fall.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ I. Be well grounded in the nature and reasons of your) Tj T*
(religion. For it is not the highest zeal and resolution that will) Tj T*
(cause you to persevere, if your judgments be not furnished with) Tj T*
(sufficient reasons to confute gainsayers, and evidence the truth, and) Tj T*
(tell you why you should persevere. I speak that with grief and shame) Tj T*
(which cannot be concealed; the number of christians is so small that) Tj T*
(are well seen in the reasons and methods of christianity, and are able) Tj T*
(to prove what they hold to be true, and to confute opposers, that it) Tj T*
(greatly afflicteth me to think, what work the atheists and infidels) Tj T*
(would make, if they once openly play their game, and be turned loose) Tj T*
(to do their worst! If they deride and oppose the immortality of the) Tj T*
(soul, and the life to come, and the truth of the Scriptures, and the) Tj T*
(work of redemption, and office of Christ; alas, how few are able to) Tj T*
(withstand them, by giving any sufficient reason of their hope! We have) Tj T*
(learnt of the papists, that he hath the strongest faith that believeth) Tj T*
(with least reason; and we have been \(truly\) taught that to deny our) Tj T*
(foundations is the horrid crime of infidelity; and therefore because) Tj T*
(it is so horrid a crime to deny or question them, we thought we need) Tj T*
(not study to prove them: and so most have taken their foundation upon) Tj T*
(trust, \(and indeed are scarce able to bear the trial of it,\) and have) Tj T*
(spent their days about the superstructure, and in learning to prove) Tj T*
(the controverted, less necessary points. Insomuch, that I fear there) Tj T*
(are more that are able to prove the points which an antinomian or an) Tj T*
(anabaptist do deny, than to prove the immortality of the soul, or the) Tj T*
(truth of Scripture, or christianity; and to dispute about a ceremony,) Tj T*
(or form of prayer, or church government, than to dispute for Christ) Tj T*
(against an infidel. So that their work is prepared to their hands, and) Tj T*
(it is no great victory to overcome such raw, unsettled souls.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ II. Get every sacred truth which you believe, into your) Tj T*
(very hearts and lives; and see that all be digested into holy love and) Tj T*
(practice. When your food is turned into vital nutriment, into flesh) Tj T*
