(to the trial for performance, nor ever call him to forsake all indeed:) Tj T*
(and therefore, if ever he be put to it, he will not perform the) Tj T*
(promise which he hath made. He is like a patient that promiseth to be) Tj T*
(wholly ruled by his physician, as hoping that he will put him upon) Tj T*
(nothing which he cannot bear. But when the bitter potion or the vomit) Tj T*
(cometh, he saith, I cannot take it, I had hoped you would have given) Tj T*
