(CHAPTER XXIX.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(DIRECTIONS FOR THE AGED \(AND WEAK\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HAVING before opened the duties of children to God, and to) Tj T*
(their parents, I shall give no other particular directions to the) Tj T*
(young, but shall next open the special duties of the aged.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ I. The old and weak have a louder call from God than) Tj T*
(others, to be accurate in examining the state of their souls, and) Tj T*
(making their calling and election sure.[125] Whether they are yet) Tj T*
(regenerate and sanctified or not, is a most important question) Tj T*
(for every man to get resolved; but especially for them that are) Tj T*
(nearest to their end. Ask counsel, therefore, of some able, faithful) Tj T*
(minister or friend, and set yourselves diligently to try your title to) Tj T*
(eternal life, and to cast up your accounts, and see how all things) Tj T*
(stand between God and you; and if you should find yourselves in an) Tj T*
(unrenewed state, as you love your souls, delay no longer, but) Tj T*
(presently be humbled for your so long and sottish neglect of so) Tj T*
(necessary and great a work. Go, open your case to some able minister,) Tj T*
(and lament your sin, and fly to Christ, and set your hearts on God, as) Tj T*
(your felicity, and change your company and course, and rest not any) Tj T*
(longer in so dangerous and miserable a case: the more full directions) Tj T*
(for your conversion I have given before, in the beginning of the book,) Tj T*
(and in divers others; and therefore shall say no more to such, it) Tj T*
(being others that I am here especially to direct.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Direct._ II. Cast back your eyes upon the sins of all your life,) Tj T*
(that you may perceive how humble those souls should be, that have) Tj T*
(sinned so long as you have done; and may feel what need you have of) Tj T*
(Christ, to pardon so long a life of sin. Though you have repented and) Tj T*
(been justified long ago, yet you have daily sinned since you were) Tj T*
(justified; and though all be forgiven that is repented of, yet must it) Tj T*
(be still before your eyes, both to keep you humble, and continue the) Tj T*
(exercise of that repentance, and drive you to Christ, and make you) Tj T*
(thankful. Yea, your forgiveness and justification are yet short of) Tj T*
(perfection, \(whatever some may tell you to the contrary,\) as well as) Tj T*
(your sanctification. For, 1. Your justification is yet given you, but) Tj T*
(conditionally as to its continuance, even upon condition of your) Tj T*
