(to future weaknesses and death. Eaten bread must not be forgotten: a) Tj T*
(thankful remembrance preserveth all your former mercies still fresh) Tj T*
(and green; the sweetness and benefit may remain, though the thing) Tj T*
(itself be past and gone. This is the great privilege of an aged) Tj T*
