() Tj T*
(DIRECTIONS FOR THE SICK.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THOUGH the chief part of our preparation for death be in the time of) Tj T*
(health, and it is a work for which the longest life is not too long;) Tj T*
(yet because the folly of unconverted sinners is so great, as to forget) Tj T*
(what they were born for till they see death at hand, and because there) Tj T*
(is a special preparation necessary for the best, I shall here lay down) Tj T*
(some directions for the sick. And I shall reduce them to these four) Tj T*
(heads: 1. What must be done to make death safe to us, that it may be) Tj T*
(our passage to heaven and not to hell. 2. What must be done to make) Tj T*
(sickness profitable to us. 3. What must be done to make death) Tj T*
(comfortable to us, that we may die in peace and joy. 4. What must be) Tj T*
(done to make our sickness profitable to others about us.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Tit. 1. Directions for a Safe Death, to secure our Salvation._) Tj T*
