(_Direct._ XI. Look back upon all the mercies of your lives, and) Tj T*
(think whence they came and what they signify. Love tokens are to draw) Tj T*
(your hearts to him that sent them; these are dropped from heaven, to) Tj T*
(entice you thither! If God have been so good to you on earth, what) Tj T*
(will he be in glory! If he so blessed you in this wilderness, what) Tj T*
(will he do in the land of promise! It greatly imboldeneth my soul to) Tj T*
(go to that God, that hath so tenderly loved me, and so graciously) Tj T*
(preserved me, and so much abounded in all sorts of mercies to me) Tj T*
(through all my life. Surely he is good that so delighteth to do good!) Tj T*
(And his presence must be sweet, when his distant mercies have been so) Tj T*
(sweet! What love shall I enjoy when perfection hath fitted me for his) Tj T*
(love, who have tasted of so much in this state of sin and imperfection!) Tj T*
(The sense of mercy will banish the fears and misgivings of the heart.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
