(I have had, since I was near to death, and since many younger than I) Tj T*
(are gone, and when I think what abundance of mercy I have had in all) Tj T*
(that time, ingenuity forbiddeth me to grudge at the season of my) Tj T*
(death, and maketh me almost ashamed to ask for longer life. How long) Tj T*
(would you stay, before, you would be willing to come to God? If he) Tj T*
(desired our company no more than we do his, and desired our happiness) Tj T*
(in heaven no more than we desire it ourselves, we should linger here) Tj T*
(as Lot in Sodom! Must we be snatched away against our wills, and) Tj T*
(carried by force to our Father's presence?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
