(body, when it is corrupted, shall at last be changed "into the) Tj T*
(likeness of Christ's glorious body, by the working of his irresistible) Tj T*
(power," Phil. iii. 20, 21. And it is a flesh that hath so rebelled) Tj T*
(against the spirit, and made your way to heaven so difficult, and put) Tj T*
