(knowledge, my sins of slothfulness, rashness, and presumption,) Tj T*
(especially those which I have wilfully committed, against thy warnings) Tj T*
(and the warnings of my conscience. Who can understand his errors?) Tj T*
(Cleanse thou me from secret sins. O pardon my unprofitableness, and) Tj T*
(abuse of thy mercies, and my sluggish loss of precious time! that I) Tj T*
(have served thee no better, and loved thee no more, and improved no) Tj T*
(better the day of grace! Though folly and sin have darkened my light,) Tj T*
(and blemished my most holy services, and my transgressions have been) Tj T*
(multiplied in thy sight, yet is the sacrifice sufficient which thou) Tj T*
(hast accepted from our great High Priest, who made his soul an) Tj T*
(offering for sin. In him thou art well pleased: he is our peace: in) Tj T*
(him I trust: he was holy, harmless, undefiled, and separate from) Tj T*
(sinners: he did no iniquity: he fulfilled all righteousness; and by) Tj T*
(once offering of himself, he hath perfected for ever them that are) Tj T*
(sanctified: he is able to save to the utmost them that come to God by) Tj T*
(him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them. Accept me, O) Tj T*
(Father, in him thy Well-beloved: let my sinful soul be healed by his) Tj T*
(stripes, who bare our sins in his body on the cross. Let me be found) Tj T*
(in him, not having any legal righteousness of my own, but that which) Tj T*
(is through the faith of Christ; that being made conformable unto) Tj T*
(his death, I may attain to the resurrection of the dead; and may by) Tj T*
(him be presented without spot or blemish. My God, thou hast encouraged) Tj T*
(my fearful soul, by the multitude of thy mercies, as well as by thy) Tj T*
(promises, to trust thee, and yield itself to thee. Thou hast filled up) Tj T*
(all my days with mercy: every place that I have lived in, and every) Tj T*
(relation, and all that I have had to do with in the world, are the) Tj T*
(witnesses of thy love and mercy to me. Thy eyes beheld my substance) Tj T*
(being yet imperfect, and all my members were written in thy book. My) Tj T*
(parents were instructed by thee to educate me, and all things) Tj T*
(commanded by thee to serve for my preservation, comfort, and) Tj T*
(salvation. Thou hast brought me forth in a land and age of mercies,) Tj T*
(and caused me to hear and see the things which others have not seen or) Tj T*
(heard. The lines have fallen to me in pleasant places; my life hath) Tj T*
(not been spent in a howling wilderness, nor in banishment from thy) Tj T*
(sanctuary, or the communion of thy saints; nor hath it been wholly) Tj T*
(consumed in darkness, and sorrow, and unserviceable barrenness. But) Tj T*
(often have I heard the joyful sound, and I have gone with the) Tj T*
(multitude to the house of God, and there have seen the light of thy) Tj T*
(countenance, and drank of the rivers of thy pleasure, even of the) Tj T*
(waters of life, and have been solaced with the voice of joy and) Tj T*
(praise. How oft have I cried unto thee in my trouble, and thou hast) Tj T*
(delivered me out of my distresses! When for my folly and transgression) Tj T*
(I was afflicted, thou broughtest me out of darkness and the shadow of) Tj T*
(death.[154] Thou renewedst my age as Hezekiah's, and causedst the) Tj T*
(shadow of my dial to go back! and hast set me at liberty to praise) Tj T*
(thee for thy goodness, and declare thy works to the children of men.) Tj T*
(In the day of trouble I called upon thee, and thou didst deliver me) Tj T*
(that I might glorify thee. Thou causedst me to receive the sentence of) Tj T*
(death, that I might trust in God that raised the dead. My Shepherd) Tj T*
ET
