(hath led me in his pleasant pastures, by the silent streams; he) Tj T*
(restored my soul, and conducted me in the paths of righteousness. How) Tj T*
(precious are thy thoughts unto me, O God! how great is the sum of) Tj T*
(them! If I should count them, they are more in number than the sand.) Tj T*
(And will that mercy now forsake me, which hath abounded to me, and) Tj T*
(supported me so long? Thou hast said, I will never fail thee nor) Tj T*
(forsake thee. Having loved thy own, that are in the world, thou wilt) Tj T*
(love them to the end; for thy mercy is great and reacheth to the) Tj T*
(heavens, and it endureth for ever. O therefore when I awake, let me be) Tj T*
(with thee! And as thy loving-kindness is better than life; and to) Tj T*
(depart and be with Christ, is far better than the best condition upon) Tj T*
(earth; so let thy servant depart in peace, his eye of faith beholding) Tj T*
(thy salvation: and when my earthly house of this tabernacle is) Tj T*
(dissolved, let me have that building of God, the house not made with) Tj T*
(hands, eternal in the heavens. Let my present burden of sin and) Tj T*
(suffering make me more earnestly to groan, not to be unclothed, but to) Tj T*
(be clothed upon, that mortality may be swallowed up of life; that) Tj T*
(being absent from the body, I may be present with the Lord.[155] And) Tj T*
(seeing this cup may not pass from me, and I must not look for the) Tj T*
(chariot of Elias, to carry me unto heaven; let thy will be done, and) Tj T*
(let me rest therein, and let death be the gain and advantage of my) Tj T*
(soul; and while this outward man is perishing, let the inner man be) Tj T*
(renewed from day to day: for what am I better than my fathers, and all) Tj T*
(thy saints, and the generations of mankind, that I should think of) Tj T*
(another passage, than this of death, to the world of immortality?[156]) Tj T*
(O let this fainting heart be glad, and let my glory rejoice, and in) Tj T*
(love and joy, in thankfulness and praise, let me pass into the world) Tj T*
(of love and joy, where thanksgiving and praise shall be my work for) Tj T*
(ever. And though my flesh and heart will fail, be thou the strength of) Tj T*
(my heart, O God, and my portion for ever.[157] Though I must walk) Tj T*
(through the valley of the shadow of death, let me fear no evil; but be) Tj T*
(thou still with me, and let me be comforted by thy rod and staff: let) Tj T*
(the goodness and mercy which hath followed me thus far all my days,) Tj T*
(receive me at the last, that I may dwell with thee for ever. For it is) Tj T*
(the will of my Redeemer, that those which thou hast given him, be with) Tj T*
(him where he is, to behold the glory which thou hast given him. And) Tj T*
(that his servants should follow him, that where he is, there also may) Tj T*
(his servants be. Amen, Lord Jesus! good is thy will and the word which) Tj T*
(thou hast spoken! Into thy hands I commend my spirit which thou hast) Tj T*
(redeemed. Receive it, and let me be with thee in paradise. O thou that) Tj T*
(hast called us thy brethren, when thou didst ascend to thy Father and) Tj T*
(our Father, and to thy God and our God, take up this poor unworthy) Tj T*
(soul to the mansions which thou hast prepared for us, that I may be) Tj T*
(with thee where thou art.[158] And though this flesh must perish, let) Tj T*
(it rest in hope, and be but sowed as a grain of wheat; till thy) Tj T*
(powerful call shall raise it from the dust, and this corruptible shall) Tj T*
(put on incorruption, and this mortal shall put on immortality, and) Tj T*
(this natural body shall be raised a spiritual body, and death shall be) Tj T*
(swallowed up in victory.[159] For though I be dead, my life is hid) Tj T*
(with Christ in God; and when thou appearest who art my life, then let) Tj T*
(me appear with thee in glory. O hasten that appearance, and come with) Tj T*
(thy holy, glorious angels, to be glorified in thy saints, and admired) Tj T*
ET
